# VitruvianSoftware Monorepo CODEOWNERS
#
# This file defines default code owners for vitruvian-core.
# Location: .github/CODEOWNERS (GitHub's preferred path).
#
# CURRENT OWNERSHIP MODEL (Single Maintainer)
# ===========================================
# The VitruvianSoftware GitHub organization currently has a SINGLE maintainer
# with login @ipv1337. All path ownership is assigned to this individual.
#
# MIGRATION TO TEAM OWNERSHIP
# =============================
# When new team maintainers are added, transition ownership as follows:
#
# 1. Create teams in the VitruvianSoftware organization:
#    - @VitruvianSoftware/devx-team        (for devx app)
#    - @VitruvianSoftware/homelab-team     (for homelab app)
#    - @VitruvianSoftware/mcp-slack-team   (for mcp-slack app)
#    - @VitruvianSoftware/nexus-agent-team (for nexus-agent app)
#    - @VitruvianSoftware/tabula-team      (for tabula app)
#    - @VitruvianSoftware/platform-team    (for platform/build/infrastructure)
#
# 2. Update CODEOWNERS paths to use team handles instead of @ipv1337, e.g.:
#    /devx/ @VitruvianSoftware/devx-team
#
# 3. For shared ownership, list multiple owners on a single line:
#    /infrastructure/ @VitruvianSoftware/platform-team @ipv1337
#
# IMPORTANT: BRANCH PROTECTION WARNING
# ======================================
# DO NOT enable "Require review from Code Owners" branch protection
# while there is only one maintainer (@ipv1337).
#
# Rationale: A solo code owner cannot approve their own pull requests.
# This would block all PRs from merging, including critical hotfixes.
# Enable it once a second maintainer / per-app team exists — which is also
# when the external-contribution model in #76 makes it load-bearing.
#
# References:
# - Issue #82: Add CODEOWNERS + enforce inter-app Bazel visibility boundaries
# - Issue #76: External-contribution model (Copybara one-way + PR-import)
#
# See https://docs.github.com/en/repositories/managing-your-repositorys-settings-and-features/customizing-your-repository/about-code-owners
# for GitHub CODEOWNERS syntax and behavior.
#
# NOTE on pattern ordering and the build-config block below:
# CODEOWNERS uses "last matching pattern wins". Build/module config patterns
# are anchored with a leading "/" so they match ONLY the repo root and do not
# accidentally re-own each app's own root BUILD file (which would otherwise be
# reassigned away from the per-app owner when teams are introduced).

# Default: catch-all for entire repository
* @ipv1337

# Application directories (per-app team scaffolding)
# ==================================================
/devx/ @ipv1337
/homelab/ @ipv1337
/mcp-slack/ @ipv1337
/nexus-agent/ @ipv1337
/tabula/ @ipv1337

# Platform, build, and infrastructure paths
# ==========================================
/tools/ @ipv1337
/infrastructure/ @ipv1337
/githooks/ @ipv1337
/.github/ @ipv1337

# Repo-root build and module configuration files
# (leading "/" anchors these to the root only; nested per-app BUILD files
#  remain owned by their app directory rule above)
# ================================================
/MODULE.bazel @ipv1337
/MODULE.bazel.lock @ipv1337
/.bazelrc @ipv1337
/.bazelversion @ipv1337
/BUILD @ipv1337
